{
  "contract": "duplicate-score-vectors",
  "version": 2,
  "enforcedBy": [
    "backend/tests/test_artisan_duplicates_scoring.py"
  ],
  "whatThisIs": [
    "THE DUPLICATE-ARTISAN SCORE, PINNED ONCE FOR BOTH PORTALS. This file is byte-identical in the designer",
    "portal and the Field Repository, and both portals' pytest read every section of it. Only the server",
    "scores (backend/app/services/artisan_duplicates.py); web and Android never do.",
    "thresholds: the show, hold and very-likely cut-offs. skeletons: the phonetic key of one word.",
    "names: name similarity (nameSim exact, or nameSimBelow an upper bound).",
    "vectors: flat profiles a and b (name, localName, gender, dateOfBirth, phone, state, district, place,",
    "village, craftId, craftCode, aadhaarFingerprint, pehchanCardNumber, remoteArtisanId). expect.score is",
    "the score before the show threshold (null when the pair is not considered at all), rounded to two",
    "decimals after adding 1e-9; expect.band is null below 0.60 (not stored); expect.reasons are the codes.",
    "pairs: score null means below the show threshold and never stored; reasons must be present and",
    "absentReasons absent. A pair using the designer portal's SAME_FIELD_REPOSITORY_LINK reason carries",
    "\"portal\": \"designer\" and is skipped in the Field Repository.",
    "Trigrams are pg_trgm's: each word padded with two spaces in front and one behind; similarity is the",
    "Jaccard of the two sets."
  ],
  "thresholds": {
    "show": 0.6,
    "hold": 0.75,
    "veryLikely": 0.9
  },
